# A deck: `deck` makes every scene after it a slide. The stage stops at the end of each slide and the viewer steps on.

deck | Why a chart beats a table
scene layout=solo mood=calm
say title | Why a chart beats a table
wait 1

scene layout=figure canvas=square
say strong | A table is read. A chart is seen.
table bars | Cups of tea a year
| Country | Cups
| Turkey | 1,300
| Ireland | 1,200
| Japan | 560
say aside | The same four numbers, and you saw the winner first.
wait 1

scene layout=page
say strong | What to take away
say | Use a table when the reader looks up one value. Use a chart when the reader compares many, or watches a thing change.
say aside | Slides end where their content does; the viewer decides when to go on.
wait 1
